{
  "schema_version": "formalization-faithfulness-1",
  "role": "adjudicator",
  "task_id": "LEV-CH01-ACOUSTICS-LEFT-MODE-CANONICAL-20260908",
  "trigger": [
    "judge classifications differ",
    "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
    "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left implication translation_implies_source unclear",
    "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear"
  ],
  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "judge classifications differ",
      "resolution": "The disagreement concerns the scope assigned to the source, not the interpretation of the Lean proposition. The target accurately represents the positive-parameter classical version. Unqualified equivalence to the selected passage remains undetermined because its admissible profile class is not specified.",
      "primary_evidence": "The inspected printed pages 1–2 display ordinary partial derivatives, permit 'any function' in the preceding scalar profile discussion, and supply no solution-space definition. The target and D007/D009 explicitly require genuine classical derivatives."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "Independent inspection confirms the acoustic equations, mode construction, speed dependence, and profile signs. The request identifies an actual source-interpretation issue; it does not reveal an incorrect dependency expansion. The two implications need not both remain unclear.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 2 gives p_t+Ku_x=0, u_t+(1/ρ)p_x=0, c=√(K/ρ), w²=p−ρcu, and w²_t−cw²_x=0. D005, D007, and the complete body of D009 reproduce these expressions."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Retain undetermined, with acceptance withheld. Equivalence holds for the physical classical interpretation, but the supplied evidence does not justify treating that interpretation as exhaustive. No faithful-stronger classification is supported: extra positivity or differentiability premises would reduce applicability if the source includes additional cases.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target assumes K>0 and ρ>0 and conditions its profile PDE on HasDerivAt. The source displays the profile family without an explicit regularity restriction. The supplied classification policy forbids counting restricted applicability as strength."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "The acoustic regularity premises faithfully express classical satisfaction of (1.5): D009 requires exactly the four displayed slice derivatives, without C1, joint differentiability, or norm bounds. Separate positivity is well motivated by the physical material interpretation, but is not a consequence of positive K/ρ alone. The direct judge's positivity conclusion therefore depends on a contextual physical convention, not solely on the displayed algebra.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 2 identifies ρ as density and K as bulk modulus and introduces positive sound speed. D008 packages ρ≠0 and global D009; the target separately assumes strict positivity of both parameters. K=ρ=−1 satisfies ρ≠0 and K/ρ>0 but fails those target premises."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "There is no change of scalar field, dimension, or coordinate domain. The only possible specializations are the positive material quadrant and classical solution concept. Both-negative coefficients are algebraically admissible, but the source's gas-or-solid interpretation does not establish them as intended material cases. Their exclusion alone is insufficient evidence for a definite weaker classification.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 1 specifies q:ℝ×ℝ→ℝ^m; page 2 specializes to two real acoustic components and a scalar mode. The explicit target specializes the generic D006/D007 codomain to Real and quantifies x,t over Real."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "No arithmetic-degeneracy defect exists on the target domain. Positive density excludes zero inversion, and positive K/ρ excludes the truncated square-root branch and zero speed. Nondifferentiable profiles are a separate coverage issue: at such characteristic arguments the target's conditional PDE assertion provides no information.",
      "primary_evidence": "D043 and D105 select real division and inverse; D051 constructs the nonnegative square root through conversion to NNReal. The target assumes K>0 and ρ>0. D020 and D007 require derivative existence rather than using a default derivative value."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "The target supplies the complete differentiable traveling-profile family and introduces neither uniqueness nor exhaustive representation. Local differentiability suffices for its local conclusion; an everywhere differentiable profile yields a global classical solution by universal instantiation. This resolves the local-versus-global objection for classical profiles. Coverage of nonsmooth solutions remains unspecified by the source.",
      "primary_evidence": "For q(x,t)=f(x+ct), a derivative f'(x+ct)=a gives q_t=ca and q_x=a, hence q_t−cq_x=0. D006 defines this same field at speed −c, and D007 existentially packages these two derivatives. Printed page 2 says the equation has solutions of the displayed form, without asserting uniqueness."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication translation_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "Lean implies every selected mathematical conclusion on the positive-parameter classical domain: acoustic decoupling, positive sound-speed magnitude, signed speed −c, and the differentiable profile family. Full source coverage remains unclear because the source does not delimit the profile solution concept.",
      "primary_evidence": "Expanding D004/D007 at −c gives w_t−cw_x=0; D005 gives p−ρcu; D006 gives f(x+ct). For a fixed profile coordinate ξ, its location is ξ−ct, which decreases for increasing time because c>0. Printed page 1's unrestricted profile wording is not matched by an unconditional classical PDE assertion."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear",
      "resolution": "Resolve this direction to yes. On inputs satisfying the target premises, the source's acoustic-mode assertion applies in its classical meaning. The profile branch is justified locally by elementary differentiation of the exact source formula, requiring no global extension, uniqueness argument, or stronger regularity. Uncertainty about additional source cases does not prevent this specialization.",
      "primary_evidence": "D008/D009 supply the classical acoustic hypotheses everywhere. For c=√(K/ρ), positivity gives c>0 and ρc²=K. The mode derivatives are p_t−ρcu_t and p_x−ρcu_x; their transport residual vanishes by (1.5). The profile derivative witnesses are ca and a, and D006 yields the exact displayed profile identity."
    },
    {
      "item": "Task-specific recheck of reused dependencies",
      "resolution": "All eight reused meanings agree with their supplied declarations and have appropriate effects here. D009 carries both acoustic equations and four derivative assertions; D011 supplies continuity infrastructure only; D019/D059 select real multiplication; D081 expresses the nonzero-density premise; D102/D105 select the real reciprocal; D109 makes real scalar multiplication ordinary multiplication. None adds a hidden equation, regularity requirement, or alternative arithmetic. This conclusion follows from the inline bodies and explicit types, not the reuse hashes.",
      "primary_evidence": "The complete dependency inventory supplies D009's existential derivative body, D011's explicit ContinuousSMul type with ordinary real topologies, and the projection or instance bodies for D019, D059, D081, D102, D105, and D109."
    },
    {
      "item": "Nonvacuity and mode/profile object identity",
      "resolution": "The theorem admits nonconstant acoustic modes and nonconstant profiles. It does not assume its mode conclusion. Its independent traveling profile is not asserted equal to the supplied system's mode, consistent with the source's solution-family wording. The printed switch from w² to q² is preserved as an unresolved editorial identification, without affecting the two separate assertions.",
      "primary_evidence": "With K=ρ=1, p(x,t)=(x+t)/2 and u(x,t)=−(x+t)/2 satisfy D009 and give w=x+t. The profile f(ξ)=ξ satisfies the profile hypothesis everywhere. Printed page 2 defines w² but uses q² in the final profile formula; the target has no equality identifying these fields."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "unclear",
      "reasoning": "The target recovers the entire positive-parameter classical claim, including acoustic linkage, the exact minus mode, positive sound-speed magnitude, negative transport coefficient, and differentiable traveling profiles. The physical context supports positive material parameters, but the source does not explicitly delimit its solution concept and inherits unrestricted profile wording. If nonsmooth solutions are included, the target does not supply that coverage. The evidence therefore supports conditional equivalence but not an unconditional coverage verdict."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "Every target system supplies the source acoustic equations with existing classical partial derivatives and positive physical parameters. The displayed mode assertion gives its scalar PDE. Positive K/ρ gives the positive principal sound speed. For the profile branch, the source formula f(x+ct), together with the supplied derivative a at x+ct, gives local slice derivatives ca and a by elementary one-variable differentiation, so the required residual is zero. D006 supplies the exact value identity. No global profile regularity, uniqueness, or identification with the given acoustic mode is required."
    }
  },
  "classification": "undetermined",
  "accepted": false,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "The source does not specify whether its unrestricted profile wording is shorthand for classical differentiable profiles or includes a nonsmooth solution concept. This affects Lean-to-source coverage.",
    "Separate material positivity is supported by the physical interpretation, but the selected pages do not explicitly delimit the coefficient domain. Both-negative pairs establish an algebraic distinction, not proof that intended physical cases were omitted."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "unresolved-source-solution-domain",
      "evidence": "Printed page 1 permits any profile in the scalar transport formula; printed page 2 repeats the traveling-profile construction without specifying regularity. The target's profile PDE conclusion requires HasDerivAt at the characteristic argument.",
      "impact": "Acceptance as an unqualified faithful representation remains unsupported. The target is faithful on the classical differentiable interpretation; any broader intended profile class would require additional coverage."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "material-domain-interpretation",
      "evidence": "The source identifies density and bulk modulus physically and uses c>0, whereas the target expressly assumes K>0 and ρ>0. Positive K/ρ alone also permits both-negative pairs.",
      "impact": "The physical convention should be distinguished from an explicitly printed hypothesis. This distinction does not by itself establish a substantive omitted source case."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "local-profile-assertion",
      "evidence": "A derivative a of f at x+ct yields derivatives ca and a of f(x+ct) in time and space at the selected point.",
      "impact": "The round-trip judge's local-versus-global concern does not block source-to-Lean implication for classical profiles."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "Inspection of the attached source renderings and exact inline declarations confirms the algebra, signs, object roles, derivative semantics, reused dependency effects, and nonvacuity. The blind translation accurately describes the target. The direct judge's equivalence verdict depends on an exhaustive physical classical reading that the selected source does not fully specify, especially for profiles. The round-trip judge correctly retains a coverage uncertainty but unnecessarily leaves the reverse implication unclear: the target's local classical assertions follow by specialization and elementary differentiation. The resulting unclear/yes implication pair consistently yields undetermined with acceptance withheld. No source or rendering hashes were independently recomputed."
}
